@squinch/pack-azure
===================

This package redistributes the Azure architecture icons.

Icon assets (icons/*.svg)
-------------------------
Copyright Microsoft Corporation. All rights reserved.

Source:  https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/architecture/icons/
Release: V24

Microsoft's published icon terms, quoted in full:

  Microsoft permits the use of these icons in architectural diagrams, training
  materials, or documentation. You can copy, distribute, and display the icons
  only for the permitted use unless granted explicit permission by Microsoft.
  Microsoft reserves all other rights.

Squinch is a tool for drawing architecture diagrams, and ships these icons for
exactly that purpose — the permitted use. That grant is what this package
relies on; it is narrower than an open-source licence, and it does not travel
to other uses. If you are building something that is not an architecture
diagram, training material, or documentation, this pack is not your licence to
use Microsoft's artwork.

Microsoft also publishes usage guidelines, which are why the files in icons/
are byte-for-byte copies of Microsoft's originals and MUST NOT be modified:

  Don't crop, flip, or rotate icons.
  Don't distort or change icon shape in any way.
  Don't use Microsoft product icons to represent your product or service.

So: not recoloured, not reshaped, not run through an SVG optimizer. Squinch
applies theme treatment at render time (placement, clipping, surrounding
plates) and never alters the asset itself. Regenerate this directory with
`npm run fetch`, never by hand.

Azure, Microsoft, and the service names and marks shown in these icons are
trademarks of Microsoft Corporation. Their use here is for identification in
architecture diagrams, the purpose Microsoft publishes them for. Squinch is not
affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Microsoft.

